Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 11:46:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(api): transactional approved/rejected provider
 notifications (MC9 commit 2)

Decision notifications are created in the SAME transaction as the
approved/rejected lifecycle event, one per event via the existing
UNIQUE(user_id, event_id) constraint (onConflictDoNothing). Shared
helper extracted to lib/application-notifications.ts and extended with
static provider-safe content; the rejected body carries no per-decision
text - the status page remains the only surface for rejectionReason.
No reviewerNotes/reviewedBy in any notification response. OpenAPI
notification type enum + regenerated clients. No web/mobile UI, no
push/email/outbox/retry. Tests land in commit 3.
